        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>SCRIP</strong> a small bag or wallet usually fastened to the girdle (1 Samuel 17:40); “a shepherd’s bag.” In the New Testament it is the rendering of Gr. pera, which was a bag carried by travellers and shepherds, generally made of skin (Matthew 10:10; Mark 6:8; Luke 9:3; 10:4). The name “scrip” is meant to denote that the bag was intended to hold scraps, fragments, as if scraped off from larger articles, trifles.",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
