        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>CRUSE</strong> a utensil; a flask or cup for holding water (1 Samuel 26:11, 12, 16; 1 Kings 19:6) or oil (1 Kings 17:12, 14, 16). In 1 Kings 14:3 the word there so rendered means properly a bottle, as in Jeremiah 19:1, 10, or pitcher. In 2 Kings 2:20, a platter or flat metal saucer is intended. The Hebrew word here used is translated “dish” in 21:13; “pans,” in 2 Chronicles 35:13; and “bosom,” in Proverbs 19:24; 26:15 (R.V., “dish”).",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
